[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  Assassin's Creed origins does a good job  of teaching you the ins and outs but  there are a few things you might miss  here are our top seven tips to become  the best assassin you can be whenever  you enter a new area make sure to unlock  all of its fast travel viewpoints not  only does it make getting across long  distances easier it also grants you a  hundred-plus experience and an increase  to send news perception skills  throughout your journey you will  accumulate a ton of loot that actually  serves no functional purpose aside from  being sold to quickly offload this junk  simply go to the cell screen of a vendor  and hold down on the d-pad to  automatically sell everything  no sorting required  [Applause]  while it might seem tempting to sell  your legendary weapon once it becomes  obsolete don't in Assassin's Creed  origins you can visit a blacksmith in  order to upgrade your weapons  and since legendary weapons carry  valuable perks it's best to hold on to  these in case you need them later on  dawn and dusk is an incredibly useful  ability that allows you to quickly pass  the time of day it's handy when you want  to attack camps at night but you don't  have enough patience to wait in addition  some quests even require you to meet  certain characters at a particular time  of day so it's in your best interest to  unlock this ability as soon as you can  similar to earlier Assassin's Creed  games you are free to exit the animus at  any time to play as the modern-day  protagonist we won't show any footage in  order to avoid spoilers but to do so  enter the pause menu and simply hold up  on the d-pad there's not much to explore  the tomb where this character is set up  shop but there is a wealth of emails and  documents you can read up on the laptop  it's worth noting that you don't  actually need to approach the computer  to access event simply press pause and  read away this is a must for hardcore  fans of the series as there's plenty of  tidbits included in these documents that  allude to past games  both weapon bear and bow bear our  abilities that let you swap between two  weapons on the fly this may not seem  useful at first but the ability to cycle  between secondary weapons becomes  indispensable during unexpected  encounters in stealth and combat for  example if a stealthy attempt at killing  a guard with your hunter bow suddenly  goes south you can instantly switch to a  light boat to quickly murder the now  alarmed foe these abilities also  eliminate the need to have to keep going  to the menu to switch out weapons  are you too lazy to ride your mount to  your current quest objective no problem  AC origins lets you set your mount to  automatically follow a path to the next  destination simply hold the X button on  Playstation or the a button on Xbox and  kick back and relax as your mount does  all the work if there's anything we  missed help out your fellow assassins in  the comments below if you want to check  out our review of Assassin's Creed  origins head on over to GameSpot comm  thanks for watching  [Music]

